{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfPjvtHnkJADY6qKAJDkp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I can't do this one safely as asked, and I want to be straight about why before you send anything to your editor.\n\n**Web search and fetch are both blocked in this session** — I tried both, and permission wasn't granted. That means every citation I could give you would come from memory, unverified. For a piece running under your name, that's the specific failure mode you don't want: plausible-looking author/title/journal/year strings that are subtly or entirely wrong. I won't produce those.\n\nHere's what I can honestly offer.\n\n## What I'm reasonably confident about (still check before print)\n\n- **Date:** Sunday 13 July 1980.\n- **Place:** Hollinwell showground, Kirkby-in-Ashfield, Nottinghamshire.\n- **Event:** an outdoor marching/jazz band and majorette contest, part of a local festival; children had been assembled in uniform since early morning in hot, humid, thundery weather.\n- **Pattern:** children collapsed in waves over several hours — fainting, dizziness, nausea, vomiting, sore eyes and throat, weakness. Adults were affected too, but far fewer.\n- **Explanations investigated:** organophosphate/pesticide drift from a nearby sprayed field (the leading early suspicion and the one parents largely believed); food poisoning; contaminated water; heat and prolonged standing; infection. The official investigation found no toxic cause sufficient to explain it and leaned toward mass sociogenic illness (\"mass hysteria\") — a conclusion that was publicly contested at the time and since.\n\n## What I do *not* trust myself on\n\n- **The casualty figure.** Numbers in the range of ~250–300 are associated with this event, but I can't reliably separate \"affected,\" \"treated on site,\" and \"taken to hospital,\" and those get conflated constantly in secondary coverage. This is your headline number — do not take it from me.\n- **Which body ran the official investigation** and what its report was formally called.\n- **Every specific citation.** I have partial recollections of the mass-sociogenic-illness literature (Simon Wessely's work in the 1980s, and a later Bartholomew & Wessely review in the *British Journal of Psychiatry*) that *may* discuss Hollinwell, but I can't confirm the volume, page, year, or whether Hollinwell appears in them at all. Printing those on my say-so would be exactly the mistake.\n\n## How to close this tonight (realistically 30–60 min)\n\n1. **Hansard** (hansard.parliament.uk, free, searchable) — search \"Hollinwell\" and \"Kirkby-in-Ashfield\" for 1980–81. If it was raised in the Commons, you get a dated, quotable primary record of the official position and the casualty figure.\n2. **PubMed** — search `Hollinwell`, then `mass sociogenic illness Nottinghamshire`, then `epidemic hysteria 1980 band contest`. Whatever returns is a real citation with a real PMID.\n3. **The BMJ archive** (bmj.com, 1980–82) — search \"Hollinwell\". Contemporaneous correspondence is likely and is highly citable.\n4. **British Newspaper Archive / Nottingham Post and Mansfield Chad** for 14–20 July 1980, plus their 40th-anniversary retrospectives (2020) — for the figure as reported at the time versus later.\n5. **Nottinghamshire Archives** hold local authority and health records; their catalogue is searchable online for the report title.\n\nRule of thumb for the piece: cite the contemporaneous record for *what happened*, and the medical literature only for *how it was later interpreted* — and attribute the \"mass hysteria\" conclusion to whoever actually reached it, rather than stating it in your own voice. The contested nature of that conclusion is arguably the story.\n\nPaste me what those searches turn up and I'll turn it into the finished fact sheet — and I can publish it as a clean page for your editor at that point. If you can enable web access in this session, I'll do the research directly instead."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":584,"cache_read_input_tokens":32343,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":584},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bc47372e-4826-464c-a5e8-d153c308a2c6","uuid":"9a3177d7-d1c8-41c6-bf1b-7236c750cdb5","timestamp":"2026-09-25T07:12:02.981Z","request_id":"req_011CfPjvsrVm1FACCbMVgeCB"}
